{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files -uuu poc/data | rg '(views\\\\.sqlite\"'$|items-comparison'\"\\\\.sqlite\"'$)'\"' | rg 'comparison-2026-11-17|/served|\"'^poc/data/views'\"'; rg -n 'served ledger|served store' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | head -n 35\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2/judge/draw-new-2/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-3/judge/draw-new-3/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-new/judge/draw-s-new/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice-2/s-old/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/slice/s-old/prod/views.sqlite\npoc/data/views.sqlite\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design for review (council round 74). No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The\\n     4\\tbehaviour is fixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first\\n     5\\tslice.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t## 0. Scope\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0.**\\n    10\\t  - The exporter `release_export`, its self-check, the package writer and the package check.\\n    11\\t  - The release builder, which calls the exporter directly.\\n    12\\t  - Tests and mutants.\\n    13\\t  - The $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    14\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    15\\t  trials. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen. This completes D756's screen check.\\n    16\\t- **Proposed for round 74: no idea submission in the release.** Today the idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step:\\n    17\\t  - `judged`, `brief`, `related_views`;\\n    18\\t  - `service.evaluate` against the ladder;\\n    19\\t  - `idea_composite.add_ladders` and the composite's endpoints.\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\t  It also calls a paid model per idea, so it needs a running service. A static release can offer no idea input at all, which fails\\n    22\\t  closed. An export-only idea path is a later slice with its own design. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only\\n    23\\t  by `v8`) moves to that slice.\\n    24\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    25\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    26\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    27\\t  - frozen pieces;\\n    28\\t  - any model call;\\n    29\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t## 1. What is built\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` (one owner, beside `service.py`):\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **Constants:**\\n    36\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    37\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    38\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`.\\n    39\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    42\\t  |---|---|\\n    43\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    44\\t  | number question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    45\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored labels, in rung order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement on or before `as_of`, or null), `evidence` |\\n    46\\t  | evidence (in force at `as_of`) | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    47\\t  | source (recorded on or before `as_of`) | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t- **`question_class(conn, view_id, rungs)`** (§3 of the design):\\n    50\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`;\\n    51\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two rung labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either\\n    52\\t    order;\\n    53\\t  - `number` otherwise. That includes a view with no key, and one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    54\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    55\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n    56\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses an unfinished first day or a future bound;\\n    57\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound, closed ones included, in `created_seq` order;\\n    58\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, never by copying a row or a bundle;\\n    59\\t  - takes evidence from `service.evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)` (in force, replacements applied, sources visible at the bound);\\n    60\\t  - takes source text from `bundle.item_lookup`;\\n    61\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning, so the writer refuses an off-list field (AGENTS §3).\\n    62\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n    63\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys; any other key fails.\\n    64\\t  - Value checks: `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants; `class` is in its set; a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n    65\\t    `answers` is two strings and `answer` is one of them or null; `open` is a bool; strings are strings.\\n    66\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n    67\\t- **`write_package(data, out_dir)`:**\\n    68\\t  - refuses an existing `out_dir`;\\n    69\\t  - writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` (`format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, the data file's sha256) into a temporary\\n    70\\t    sibling, then renames it into place, so a crash leaves no half package.\\n    71\\t- **`check_package(out_dir)`:**\\n    72\\t  - the directory holds exactly `{manifest.json, release-data.json}` (slice 2 adds the page), with no subdirectories;\\n    73\\t  - the manifest's sha256 matches the data file;\\n    74\\t  - the data passes `check_export`;\\n    75\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n    76\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`:** for the release check report only. It lists the number questions whose ladder does not\\n    77\\t  resolve (`service.ladder_bands` returns None), with or without a key. They are withheld like every number question (design §3).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\t`scripts/release_build.py --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:\\n    80\\t- calls `release.release_export` directly; there is no input path for prepared or translated JSON;\\n    81\\t- then `write_package`, then `check_package`;\\n    82\\t- prints the counts and the unresolved list, and writes the same report to `<out>.report.json` beside the package, never inside it;\\n    83\\t- takes no clock reading. The folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n    88\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n    89\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `resolve_bound` raises `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n    90\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | the requested day |\\n    91\\t| `--as-of` omitted | the last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n    92\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n    93\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`; no reason and no closing day | — | bound (`is_open_as_of`) |\\n    94\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n    95\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n    96\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n    97\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n    98\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded from `sources` | — | bound |\\n    99\\t| Store being written by a live run | not supported: the builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9); both connections are pinned for the export | — | — |\\n   100\\t| `out_dir` exists | refused before any write | nothing | — |\\n   101\\t| Crash midway through writing | the temporary sibling is left; `out_dir` does not exist | temp folder only | — |\\n   102\\t| Two builds of one store | each needs a new folder; the second never overwrites | — | — |\\n   103\\t| Configuration or store changed between builds | each package records its `as_of` and the data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   104\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys`, Chinese labels | no key, so no event; `是`/`否` canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   105\\t| Off-list key reaches the record | `check_export` raises inside `release_export`; nothing is written | nothing | — |\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\tReaders of the package:\\n   110\\t- `check_package`;\\n   111\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   112\\t- the tests.\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\tNo POC reader reads it: no service, MCP, `bundle` or `idea` code imports `release`.\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t| Value | Source (table.column) | Note |\\n   117\\t|---|---|---|\\n   118\\t| `id`, `object`, `kind`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `object_id`, `kind`, `question` | `question` is allowed by D726 |\\n   119\\t| `open` | `view_switches.open` via `service.is_open_as_of` | `reason` never read |\\n   120\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | identity only |\\n   121\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label`; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | non-number only |\\n   122\\t| evidence fields | `evidence.*`, `evidence_links`, `replacements` via `service.evidence` | sources recorded and visible at the bound |\\n   123\\t| source fields | `evidence_sources.publication_day`; items `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri` | — |\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t**Never read** by `release_export`:\\n   126\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   127\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   128\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   129\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   130\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   131\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`;\\n   132\\t- every count and every date of a judgement.\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\tThe one exception is `judgements.rung` for non-number questions. The report-only `withheld_unresolved` reads rungs, but its output\\n   135\\tnever enters the package.\\n   136\\t\\n   137\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   140\\t|---|---|\\n   141\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   142\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   143\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence` |\\n   144\\t| Pinned read transaction for a complete envelope | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   145\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read: no new failure mode |\\n   146\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused (`LedgerError`) | no JSON column read |\\n   147\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields (`thesis-ui/2`) | the release has its own contract (`check_export`); the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   152\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   153\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   154\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   155\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   156\\t- D163: English product text. Stored labels are emitted as stored; a legacy Chinese ledger is not a release input.\\n   157\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   158\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path, built with `store.create_view` and `store.insert`. Each test names its row above:\\n   163\\t1. **Allow-list (§1):**\\n   164\\t   - every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys;\\n   165\\t   - positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   166\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. The serialized export contains no rung label, condition, judgement reason\\n   167\\t   or `why_changed` text of that view. This is the decisive assertion.\\n   168\\t3. **Number with bounds only in its conditions** (no key): `number`.\\n   169\\t4. **Unresolved number with a key** (a money measure, no bounds, unreadable conditions): `number`, and listed by\\n   170\\t   `withheld_unresolved`.\\n   171\\t5. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate`, labels Yes/No). Its answer label is shown. Its `why_changed` quoting \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is\\n   172\\t   absent.\\n   173\\t6. **Event:** the label is kept. A `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   174\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   175\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds.\\n   176\\t9. **Package:**\\n   177\\t   - write, then check, passes;\\n   178\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   179\\t   - a changed data byte fails the sha check;\\n   180\\t   - an existing `out_dir` is refused.\\n   181\\t10. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted) on the fixture store. The package passes the\\n   182\\t    check and the report lists the unresolved view.\\n   183\\t11. **Legacy labels** `是`/`否`: `yes_no`.\\n   184\\t\\n   185\\t**Mutants,** run on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   186\\t- an off-list field emitted (`condition` on a number record);\\n   187\\t- the event test removed;\\n   188\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   189\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   190\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   191\\t- the switch reason emitted.\\n   192\\t\\n   193\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   196\\tserved ledger.\\n   197\\t1. **Whole-store leak sweep.** For every view, collect the strings the package must not hold:\\n   198\\t   - for a number question: rung labels and conditions, judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons;\\n   199\\t   - for any other question: judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, switch reasons.\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t   Search the serialized export for each string of at least 12 characters, then report how many strings were judged and every hit,\\n   202\\t   read by hand.\\n   203\\t2. **`old-1/v8`.** The record has the marker and the same evidence ids and sources as `service.evidence` at the bound. None of its 5\\n   204\\t   labels, its 75 judgements' texts or its band is in the package.\\n   205\\t3. **`old-3/v36` (j799) and `old-1/v10` (j865).** Labels kept; the \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text absent.\\n   206\\t4. **Control.** One unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   207\\t5. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a real closing switch for `v8` in the store's own reason format (\\\"due …, frozen\\n   208\\t   on … at rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the band there, then confirm the package does not.\\n   209\\t6. **Size and speed:** export bytes and seconds against `bundle.library` on the same store.\\n   210\\t\\n   211\\t## 8. Open for round 74\\n   212\\t\\n   213\\t1. **The idea path:** none in the release (§0)? Or must slice 1 include an export-only idea path?\\n   214\\t2. **`object` and `kind` on every record.** They are not in the design's list (\\\"the question and its id\\\"). They are identity, not a\\n   215\\t   forecast, and the library groups by object. Keep them, or drop them?\\n   216\\t3. **Research groups** (`thesis_groups`: model-written names and scopes) are left out. Is that right for slice 1?\\n   217\\t4. **The leak sweep's 12-character floor.** Is it right, and is any string class missing from the sweep?\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | tail -n +58; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n     1\\t1. Revision 4 adds the package boundary and acceptance case that 72c requested. The builder must call the exporter directly, and the check covers the finished package. The `old-1/v8` idea card must show its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” with no scored driver or substitute band. The same package must preserve both event labels and omit their spending forecasts. I found no unrelated change. [Revision 3 snapshot:15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:15) · [Design:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:37) · [Design:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:129)\\n     2\\t2. One prose rule now covers events and Yes/No questions, including all 85 overlapping cases. The figures match 72c. Option (b) would preserve explanations for 21 of 85 latest answers and 73 of 73 historical answers in the sealed ledger. The design recommends (a) to Alex. Under (a), I found no remaining route in the design for a stored number forecast to reach a release reader. [72c:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:5) · [Design:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Design:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:98)\\n     3\\t3. **One correction from 72c is incomplete.** Line 97 still tells Alex that an explanation kept under (b) “cannot quote a number forecast.” Line 102 correctly says it can. A Yes/No answer can repeat a spending forecast from its previous explanation even when the current request shows no number question directly. Delete the sentence spanning lines 96–97 that makes the guarantee. [Design:96](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:96) · [Design:102](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:102) · [judging.py:211](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:211)\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** The contradictory guarantee is the only blocker. Once removed, the design is ready to hand to release work when Alex opens it, with §4’s choice still his and **(a) recommended**.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:196:served ledger.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:59:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_30\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/README.md\\nrg -n 'Restriction adopted|No restriction adopted' docs scripts tests poc --glob '\\\"'!*.stream'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.json*'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.html'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.out'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.csv'\\\"' | head -20\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# Served copy of the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger, minus v68\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t`views.sqlite` = `sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` with thesis v68 removed (Alex, 2026-10-28 17:05:\\n     4\\t\\\"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\\\"). v68, \\\"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\\\", was opened on the\\n     5\\trun's last day by the succession rule (same quantity, next period, after v24) and the writer linked its one opening statement to\\n     6\\tv7 and v24 instead of to it, so it stood with no evidence and no judgement. Rows removed: views, view_keys, rungs, successions,\\n     7\\tview_switches, views_fts for v68 (no evidence_links or judgements existed). The sealed folder is untouched and remains the record;\\n     8\\tthe front end, the API and the page build read this copy.\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3509:- Alex, after the browser check showed v49's state as \\\"No No restriction adopted\\\": \\\"修，然后 merge main\\\".\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510:- Mechanism: the state chip and the chart's spoken text join the score and the rung label. A two-rung ladder's score is Yes/No; when the ladder names its outcomes (06-views allows named outcomes for yes/no theme theses), the label repeats it. Census: 1 of 55 two-rung theses in the served ledger (v49: Restriction adopted / No restriction adopted) and 1 in the 2026-10-27 snapshot (Permission granted / Permission not granted).\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3512:- Result: the D336 UI test fails on the old composition (\\\"No No restriction adopted\\\"); 58 UI tests, lint, format and the 20 standing UI mutation checks pass. In headless Chrome, with the cache disabled, v49 shows \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" and v14 \\\"Yes\\\".\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:302:  named.rungs[0].label = 'Restriction adopted';\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:303:  named.rungs[1].label = 'No restriction adopted';\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:308:  assert.equal(stateText(thesis, 2), 'No restriction adopted');\\npoc/ui/test/composite.test.js:311:    '<span class=\\\"chip chip--state state--negative\\\"><b>No restriction adopted</b></span>',\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:80:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_41\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"1. **The single export closes the old routes if the release builder takes its data only from that exporter.** That covers the idea card, both places where its summary re-reads the ladder, the closing sentence, the live `/library` reload, translated JSON and composite trials. One detail still matters at handoff. A marker and version identify a format. They cannot establish who supplied the text in an allowed field. Have the builder call the exporter directly, and check the finished package as well as the page. The current builder accepts external JSON, embeds market data and trials separately, and writes beside the translated export. A page can make zero fetches while its package still contains the unrestricted file. [Design §2:35](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20) · [mock_build.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:54) · [mock_translate.py:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:129) · [idea.py:346](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:346)\\n\\n2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\n\\n3. **Recommend (a) for the first release. Option (b) is measurable, but §4 overstates what it proves.** I matched each Yes/No judgement to its archived request by call ID and request hash. Counting requests with no directly shown number-question state, (b) would keep **31/769**, **44/776** and **43/958** explanations across the three comparison runs. For a reader viewing the latest answer, it would keep explanations on **21/85 questions**. It would also keep **73/73** historical explanations in the sealed ledger. That is the benefit Alex would give up under (a). The limit is that a request also includes the question’s previous reasoning and can include another Yes/No question’s reasoning. Either can carry a forecast it saw earlier. Checking the current request for a directly shown number question cannot justify §4’s promise that the explanation “cannot quote a number forecast.” Both known disclosures are specifically in `why_changed`, including “around $1 trillion” in `old-3/v36`. [Design §4:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:84) · [archived requests:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:40) · [judgement-to-request link:308](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:308) · [reasoning copied into requests:202](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:202) · [stored cases:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27)\\n\\n4. **Before handoff, write one end-to-end acceptance case around what the reader gets.** Use `old-1/v8` as the only question in an idea. Its sources and “Forecast unavailable” must survive onto the card, with no scored driver and no invented replacement band. This matters because the current idea code expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate. In the same release package, verify that the two known event answers retain their labels and omit the spending forecasts under Alex’s chosen prose rule. Keep the design’s separate real closing-switch check. This review was read-only and cost $0. [idea_composite.py:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:214) · [idea_composite.py:231](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:231) · [design acceptance:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:115) · [Alex’s release decision:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833)\\n\\n**Verdict — not ready as written.** Keep the single exporter and §3. Make the package boundary enforceable, apply one prose rule across overlapping event and Yes/No questions, and put the measured trade-off to Alex with **(a)** recommended.\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:3:2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:86:binary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r73.stream:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n    97\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    98\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n    99\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   100\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   101\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   102\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   103\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   104\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   105\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   110\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   111\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   112\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   113\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   114\\t  - an event question;\\n   115\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   116\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   117\\t  - an idea.\\n   118\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   119\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   120\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   121\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   122\\t  - an extra field;\\n   123\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   124\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   125\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t  Each must fail.\\n   128\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   129\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   130\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   131\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   132\\t    prose rule.\\n   133\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   134\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   135\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   136\\t    final band there.\\n   137\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   138\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   139\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   144\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   145\\t- Other open defects.\\n   146\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   147\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:11:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t1. **The single export closes the old routes if the release builder takes its data only from that exporter.** That covers the idea card, both places where its summary re-reads the ladder, the closing sentence, the live `/library` reload, translated JSON and composite trials. One detail still matters at handoff. A marker and version identify a format. They cannot establish who supplied the text in an allowed field. Have the builder call the exporter directly, and check the finished package as well as the page. The current builder accepts external JSON, embeds market data and trials separately, and writes beside the translated export. A page can make zero fetches while its package still contains the unrestricted file. [Design §2:35](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:35) · [mock_build.py:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:20) · [mock_build.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:54) · [mock_translate.py:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:129) · [idea.py:346](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:346)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t3. **Recommend (a) for the first release. Option (b) is measurable, but §4 overstates what it proves.** I matched each Yes/No judgement to its archived request by call ID and request hash. Counting requests with no directly shown number-question state, (b) would keep **31/769**, **44/776** and **43/958** explanations across the three comparison runs. For a reader viewing the latest answer, it would keep explanations on **21/85 questions**. It would also keep **73/73** historical explanations in the sealed ledger. That is the benefit Alex would give up under (a). The limit is that a request also includes the question’s previous reasoning and can include another Yes/No question’s reasoning. Either can carry a forecast it saw earlier. Checking the current request for a directly shown number question cannot justify §4’s promise that the explanation “cannot quote a number forecast.” Both known disclosures are specifically in `why_changed`, including “around $1 trillion” in `old-3/v36`. [Design §4:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:84) · [archived requests:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:40) · [judgement-to-request link:308](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:308) · [reasoning copied into requests:202](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:202) · [stored cases:27](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:27)\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t4. **Before handoff, write one end-to-end acceptance case around what the reader gets.** Use `old-1/v8` as the only question in an idea. Its sources and “Forecast unavailable” must survive onto the card, with no scored driver and no invented replacement band. This matters because the current idea code expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate. In the same release package, verify that the two known event answers retain their labels and omit the spending forecasts under Alex’s chosen prose rule. Keep the design’s separate real closing-switch check. This review was read-only and cost $0. [idea_composite.py:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:214) · [idea_composite.py:231](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:231) · [design acceptance:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:115) · [Alex’s release decision:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833)\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t**Verdict — not ready as written.** Keep the single exporter and §3. Make the package boundary enforceable, apply one prose rule across overlapping event and Yes/No questions, and put the measured trade-off to Alex with **(a)** recommended.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:13:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n     4\\t- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n     5\\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n     6\\t- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n    11\\tcould reach a reader:\\n    12\\t- the idea card;\\n    13\\t- the closing text;\\n    14\\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n    15\\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n    16\\t- a translated export;\\n    17\\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\n    20\\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n    25\\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n    26\\t- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n    27\\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n    28\\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n    29\\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n    36\\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n    37\\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n    38\\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n    39\\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n    40\\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n    41\\t  - no live POC service;\\n    42\\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n    43\\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n    44\\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n    47\\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n    48\\t  - the question and its id;\\n    49\\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n    50\\t  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t  Nothing else is listed:\\n    53\\t  - no ladder;\\n    54\\t  - no band, label or condition;\\n    55\\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n    56\\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n    57\\t  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n    58\\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n    59\\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n    60\\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n    61\\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n    62\\t  delivered card.\\n    63\\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n    64\\t  later choice for Alex.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n    69\\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n    70\\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n    71\\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n    72\\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n    73\\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n    76\\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n    77\\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n    80\\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n    81\\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n    86\\tbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n    87\\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\n    92\\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n    93\\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n    94\\t  readers would see.\\n    95\\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n    96\\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown). It keeps the reasoning where it\\n    97\\t  cannot quote a number forecast.\\n    98\\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n    99\\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n   100\\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n   101\\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n   102\\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n   103\\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n   104\\t  `why_changed`.\\n   105\\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n   106\\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n   109\\t\\n   110\\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n   111\\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n   112\\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n   113\\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n   114\\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n   115\\t  - an event question;\\n   116\\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n   117\\t  - a real closing switch;\\n   118\\t  - an idea.\\n   119\\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n   120\\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n   121\\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n   122\\t- **Mutants:**\\n   123\\t  - an extra field;\\n   124\\t  - a fetch left on;\\n   125\\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n   126\\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t  Each must fail.\\n   129\\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n   130\\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n   131\\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n   132\\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n   133\\t    prose rule.\\n   134\\t- **The $0 release check.**\\n   135\\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n   136\\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n   137\\t    final band there.\\n   138\\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n   139\\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n   140\\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t## 6. Not in scope\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n   145\\t- The closed v13s line.\\n   146\\t- Other open defects.\\n   147\\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n   148\\t- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72d.stream:40:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib,difflib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\\\\\\\"); s=json.loads((p/\\\\\\\"codex-r72c.stream\\\\\\\").read_text().splitlines()[14])[\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\"][\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\"]; a=[l.split(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\",1)[1] for l in s.splitlines()]; b=(p/\\\\\\\"FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\\\\\").read_text().splitlines();print(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,n=0)))'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"--- \\n\\n+++ \\n\\n@@ -10 +10 @@\\n\\n-**Revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n+**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\n@@ -36,0 +37,3 @@\\n\\n+- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n+  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n+  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n@@ -82 +85,5 @@\\n\\n-## 4. Yes/No questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n+**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\n+binary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\n+every question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n+\\n+## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n@@ -91,2 +98,9 @@\\n\\n-- **Claude's lean is (b).** It keeps value and is decided by structure. It needs a $0 census of how many Yes/No judgements it keeps\\n-  on the stored stores before release.\\n+- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n+  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n+  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n+  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n+- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n+  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n+  `why_changed`.\\n+- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n+  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n@@ -114,0 +129,5 @@\\n\\n+- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n+  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n+    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n+  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n+    prose rule.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | head -n 248'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | head -n 248'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\n     2\tevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\n     3\tswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\n     4\tend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\"\"\"\n     5\timport json\n     6\tfrom contextlib import contextmanager\n     7\tfrom datetime import date\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom . import service\n    10\tfrom .views import store\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t@contextmanager\n    14\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\n    15\t    \"\"\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\"\"\"\n    16\t    owned = []\n    17\t    try:\n    18\t        for conn in connections:\n    19\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\n    20\t                conn.execute('begin')\n    21\t                owned.append(conn)\n    22\t        yield\n    23\t    finally:\n    24\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\n    25\t            conn.rollback()\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\n    29\t    \"\"\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\n    30\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\"\"\"\n    31\t    cache = {}\n    32\t\n    33\t    def item_of(input_id):\n    34\t        if input_id not in cache:\n    35\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\n    36\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\n    37\t        return cache[input_id]\n    38\t    return item_of\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\n    42\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\n    46\t    \"\"\"The view's ladder as the new system's writer stored it (`clean_ladders`, written in the view's own call): the parsed\n    47\t    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\n    48\t    view. A row that is not readable JSON with a ladder, or two rows for one view, is refused.\"\"\"\n    49\t    if not views_db.execute(\"select 1 from sqlite_master where type='table' and name='clean_ladders'\").fetchone():\n    50\t        return 'no table'\n    51\t    rows = views_db.execute('select checked_answer from clean_ladders where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    52\t    if not rows:\n    53\t        return 'no row'\n    54\t    if len(rows) > 1:\n    55\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: {len(rows)} ladder rows for one view')\n    56\t    try:\n    57\t        ladder = json.loads(rows[0][0])['ladder']\n    58\t    except (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError) as error:\n    59\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder ({error!r})')\n    60\t    if not isinstance(ladder, dict):\n    61\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder')\n    62\t    return ladder\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef not_judged(views_db, view_id, created_seq, as_of=None):\n    66\t    \"\"\"D397: the parts of a topic its one judged question leaves out, with their reasons, from the view's ladder row. None for a\n    67\t    legacy ledger, for a view with no row, and before the view's creation at as_of; [] when the row lists none. A malformed row,\n    68\t    or two rows for one view, is refused. Called directly for a view not visible at the resolved bound, it refuses the view\n    69\t    (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3), so a question created after that day is never returned.\"\"\"\n    70\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\n    71\t    if as_of is not None and not _visible(views_db, created_seq, as_of):\n    72\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\n    73\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\n    74\t    if ladder in ('no table', 'no row'):\n    75\t        return None\n    76\t    parts = ladder.get('not_judged')\n    77\t    if not isinstance(parts, list) or not all(isinstance(p, dict) and isinstance(p.get('part'), str) and isinstance(p.get('why'), str) for p in parts):\n    78\t        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its parts not judged are not a list of {{part, why}} texts')\n    79\t    return [{'part': p['part'], 'why': p['why']} for p in parts]\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef answer_shape(views_db, view_id):\n    83\t    \"\"\"(shape, favourable end) of the view's answer choices, as the page needs them to read the stored labels without inventing a\n    84\t    direction (page-contract/DESIGN.md): (None, None) for a legacy ledger; ('unrecorded', None) for a view with no row in a store\n    85\t    that has rows; ('event', None) or ('figure', 'higher' | 'lower' | 'n/a') from the row. Not suppressed before creation: it says\n    86\t    how to read the labels, which are shown as they are.\"\"\"\n    87\t    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\n    88\t    if ladder == 'no table':\n    89\t        return None, None\n    90\t    if ladder == 'no row':\n    91\t        return 'unrecorded', None\n    92\t    if ladder.get('event'):\n    93\t        return 'event', None\n    94\t    figure = ladder.get('figure')\n    95\t    if isinstance(figure, dict) and figure.get('favourable_end') in ('higher', 'lower', 'n/a'):\n    96\t        return 'figure', figure['favourable_end']\n    97\t    raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row is neither an event nor a figure with a favourable end')\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tdef view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\n   101\t    \"\"\"One view's complete record as of the bound (resolved; an omitted bound on a store with no completed day reads every\n   102\t    record, as before). A view not visible at the bound is refused (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\"\"\"\n   103\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\n   104\t    v = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   105\t    if v is None:\n   106\t        raise KeyError(view_id)\n   107\t    if as_of is not None and not service.view_exists(views_db, v, as_of):\n   108\t        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\n   109\t    columns = {r[1] for r in views_db.execute('pragma table_info(rungs)')}\n   110\t    bounds = ', lo, hi' if {'lo', 'hi'} <= columns else ''          # a ledger written before keys has no bounds; the adapter then reads the prose\n   111\t    rungs = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute(f'select position, label, condition{bounds} from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\n   112\t    switches = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,))\n   113\t                if _visible(views_db, r['after_seq'], as_of)]\n   114\t    for switch in switches:\n   115\t        switch['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, switch['after_seq'])\n   116\t    judgements = []\n   117\t    for j in views_db.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\n   118\t        if as_of is not None and j['publication_day'] > as_of:\n   119\t            continue\n   120\t        judgements.append({'id': str(j['judgement_id']), 'day': j['publication_day'], 'seq': j['seq'], 'rung': j['rung'], 'changed': bool(j['changed']),\n   121\t                           'why_changed': j['why_changed'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'cited': list(dict.fromkeys(json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json'] or '[]'))),   # each id once (UI contract uniqueItems); the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger holds one judgement citing an id twice\n   122\t                           'cited_views': json.loads(j['cited_views_json'] or '[]'), 'pushes': json.loads(j['pushes_json'] or '[]'),\n   123\t                           'from_item': j['input_id']})\n   124\t    evidence = []\n   125\t    for e in views_db.execute('select e.*, l.seq as linked_seq from evidence_links l join evidence e on e.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by l.id', (view_id,)):\n   126\t        if not _visible(views_db, e['linked_seq'], as_of):\n   127\t            continue\n   128\t        sources = [dict(s) for s in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (e['evidence_id'],))\n   129\t                   if _visible(views_db, s['seq'], as_of)]\n   130\t        replaced_by = views_db.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n   131\t        if replaced_by is not None and not _visible(views_db, replaced_by['seq'], as_of):\n   132\t            replaced_by = None\n   133\t        replaces = views_db.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n   134\t        if replaces and not _visible(views_db, replaces['seq'], as_of):\n   135\t            replaces = None\n   136\t        first = sources[0] if sources else {'input_id': e['created_from_input'], 'publication_day': '', 'seq': e['created_seq']}\n   137\t        item = item_of(first['input_id'])\n   138\t        evidence.append({'id': e['evidence_id'], 'one_line': e['one_line'], 'quote': e['quote'], 'tier': e['tier'], 'speaker': e['speaker'],\n   139\t                         'original_who': e['original_who'], 'original_day': e['original_day'], 'event_time': e['event_time'],\n   140\t                         'day': first['publication_day'] or item['publication_day'], 'seq': first['seq'], 'linked_seq': e['linked_seq'],\n   141\t                         'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, e['linked_seq']),\n   142\t                         'source': {'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'publisher_type': item['publisher_type'],\n   143\t                                    'category': item['category'], 'uri': item['source_uri']},\n   144\t                         'sources': [{'input_id': s['input_id'], 'day': s['publication_day'],\n   145\t                                      'arrival_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, s['seq']),\n   146\t                                      'source': item_of(s['input_id'])} for s in sources],\n   147\t                         'outlets': len(sources), 'replaced_by': {'new_evidence_id': replaced_by['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': replaced_by['said_day'],\n   148\t                                                               'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, replaced_by['seq'])} if replaced_by else None,\n   149\t                         'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces else None})\n   150\t    dependencies = [dict(r) for r in views_db.execute('select dependency_id, depends_on, direction, wait_chain_view_id, wait_year, seq from dependencies where view_id=? order by dependency_id', (view_id,))\n   151\t                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\n   152\t    for dependency in dependencies:\n   153\t        dependency['day'] = service.day_of_seq(views_db, dependency['seq'])\n   154\t        dependency['resolutions'] = [dict(target=r['resolved_to'], day=service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq']), seq=r['seq'])\n   155\t                                    for r in views_db.execute('select resolved_to, seq from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=? order by id', (dependency['dependency_id'],))\n   156\t                                    if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\n   157\t    dependants = sorted({r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select view_id, seq from dependencies where depends_on=?', (view_id,)) if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)},\n   158\t                        key=lambda s: (len(s), s))\n   159\t    created = item_of(v['created_from_input'])\n   160\t    key = store.view_key(views_db, view_id)\n   161\t    identity = {name: key[name] for name in ('measure', 'scope', 'period_start', 'period_end', 'basis', 'unit', 'event_type')} if key else None\n   162\t    successions = [{'thesis_id': r['succeeds'] if r['view_id'] == view_id else r['view_id'],\n   163\t                    'relation': 'previous' if r['view_id'] == view_id else 'next',\n   164\t                    'day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, r['seq'])}\n   165\t                   for r in views_db.execute('select * from successions where view_id=? or succeeds=? order by id', (view_id, view_id))\n   166\t                   if _visible(views_db, r['seq'], as_of)]\n   167\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'object': v['object_id'], 'kind': v['kind'], 'looks_at': v['looks_at'], 'question': v['question'],\n   168\t            'due_day': v['due_day'], 'year': v['year'], 'identity': identity, 'successions': successions,\n   169\t            'created_seq': v['created_seq'], 'created_day': service.day_of_seq(views_db, v['created_seq']),\n   170\t            'created_from': {'title': created['title'], 'publisher': created['publisher'], 'category': created['category']},\n   171\t            'rungs': rungs, 'open': not any(not s['open'] for s in switches), 'switches': switches,\n   172\t            'judgements': judgements, 'evidence': evidence, 'dependencies': dependencies, 'dependants': dependants,\n   173\t            'not_judged': not_judged(views_db, view_id, v['created_seq'], as_of),\n   174\t            **dict(zip(('answer_shape', 'favourable_end'), answer_shape(views_db, view_id)))}\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\tdef days(views_db, as_of=None):\n   178\t    \"\"\"The completed days the front end's time axis runs over, up to as_of.\"\"\"\n   179\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\n   180\t    return [r[0] for r in views_db.execute('select day from days_completed order by day') if as_of is None or r[0] <= as_of]\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\tdef _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\n   184\t    \"\"\"Complete, dated UI inputs for caller-selected theses; no search, model call or ledger write. Its bound is already resolved\n   185\t    by its caller (`thesis_bundles`, `library`).\"\"\"\n   186\t    date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   187\t    if not isinstance(view_ids, list) or not view_ids or any(not isinstance(id, str) or not id for id in view_ids):\n   188\t        raise ValueError('thesis_bundles needs a non-empty list of view ids')\n   189\t    lookup = item_lookup(items_db)\n   190\t    records = []\n   191\t    for view_id in dict.fromkeys(view_ids):\n   192\t        row = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   193\t        if row is None or not service.view_exists(views_db, row, as_of):\n   194\t            raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\n   195\t        records.append(view_bundle(views_db, lookup, view_id, as_of))\n   196\t    return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': records,\n   197\t            'coverage': coverage, 'groups': research_groups(views_db, view_ids, as_of)}\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\tdef research_groups(conn, view_ids, as_of):\n   201\t    \"\"\"Stored groups, with dated memberships limited to the envelope's loaded theses.\"\"\"\n   202\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_groups)').fetchone():\n   203\t        return []\n   204\t    loaded = set(view_ids)\n   205\t    result = []\n   206\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from thesis_groups order by created_seq, rowid'):\n   207\t        if not service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of):\n   208\t            continue\n   209\t        members = [{'thesis_id': m['view_id'], 'day': service.day_of_seq(conn, m['seq']), 'basis': m['basis'] or ''}\n   210\t                   for m in conn.execute('select * from thesis_group_members where group_id=? order by id', (row['group_id'],))\n   211\t                   if m['view_id'] in loaded and service.visible(conn, m['seq'], as_of)]\n   212\t        if members:\n   213\t            result.append({'id': row['group_id'], 'name': row['name'], 'scope': row['scope'],\n   214\t                           'aliases': json.loads(row['aliases'] or '[]') if 'aliases' in row.keys() else [],\n   215\t                           'created_day': service.day_of_seq(conn, row['created_seq']), 'members': members})\n   216\t    return result\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\tdef thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\n   220\t    \"\"\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\"\"\"\n   221\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   222\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n   226\t    \"\"\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\"\"\"\n   227\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   228\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n   229\t        if not as_of:\n   230\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\n   231\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   232\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\n   233\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\n   234\t        if not view_ids:\n   235\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\n   236\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
