{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\b(add_evidence|evidence_record)\\\\(' src; rg -n '(served.*views.sqlite|HIVEMIND_LEDGER|--ledger)' README.md | head -n 35; rg -n 'served ledger|served store' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{codex-r72b.md,codex-r72c.md,round74-brief.md}\"","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/baseline.py:207:                store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=f['quote'], one_line=one_line_of(f), speaker=item['publisher'],\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:224:def evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:248:        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:358:        cited = [piece for piece in (evidence_record(conn, e, row['publication_day']) for e in _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json']))) if piece]\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:355:def add_evidence(conn, *, evidence_id, quote, one_line, speaker, original_who, original_day, tier, event_time, seq, input_id):\nsrc/hivemind/views/writing.py:31:    store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=e['quote'], one_line=e['one_line'], speaker=e['speaker'],\n93:| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\n107:| `scripts/mock_build.py` | `--ledger` and `--items` defaults, then `python3 scripts/mock_build.py` rebuilds `poc/mock/index.html` |\n159:  --views /absolute/path/to/preserved/views.sqlite \\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.md:3:2. **§3 classified the stored questions correctly.** I independently found 19, 17 and 18 number questions in the three comparison stores. In the sealed ledger, withholding covered 43 money questions and 21 other numeric questions. All 30 Chinese Yes/No pairs were recognized. The Xbox question correctly kept its Yes/No answer despite having bounds around zero. One distinction matters for release prose. **All 85 comparison-store events are also Yes/No questions**, including both known leaks. The §4 prose rule must apply to them even when the event check matches first. The served ledger also has a binary event labeled “Restriction adopted” and “No restriction adopted.” Its existing answer label should remain usable under the same prose rule. [Design §3:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [named event decision:3510](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3510)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
