{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba README.md | sed -n '87,105p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | head -n 110; nl -ba src/hivemind/baseline.py | sed -n '163,225p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/idea.py | sed -n '115,146p;215,279p'\"","aggregated_output":"    87\tUse Python 3.12 or later for the backend and Node.js 22 or later with npm for frontend builds. The HTTP service uses the Python standard library. The optional MCP service needs `mcp==1.26.0`. Frontend development dependencies are locked in `poc/ui/package-lock.json`.\n    88\t\n    89\tThe default backend reads these local files:\n    90\t\n    91\t| Purpose | Path |\n    92\t|---|---|\n    93\t| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\n    94\t| Source items | `poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` (cleaned pages, D351, with the whole pages as fetched in column `text_page`; also kept apart in `items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.page.sqlite`) |\n    95\t| Replay configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118.json` (D370): v108 extraction, matching and judging settings without seeded starting questions or separate report import |\n    96\t| Idea configuration | `poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json`: two discovery calls and a final adoption/weighting call |\n    97\t| Derived service index and Idea archive | `poc/data/service-english/` by default; overridable per run |\n    98\t\n    99\t`poc/data/` is excluded from Git. A fresh clone includes the standalone demo, not these databases. Use the [data manifest](docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md) to locate preserved runs, or supply your own files with the documented CLI options. Keep provider credentials in the owner-only local file `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository.\n   100\t\n   101\t### Switching the served data\n   102\t\n   103\tThe page build, the two services and Compose each carry the same two defaults: the thesis ledger (`views.sqlite`) and the items database the ledger's input ids come from. Swap both together; a ledger whose items are missing shows evidence without titles or sources. Serve a copy of a ledger a run may still write (`snapshot.sh` in a run folder makes one with SQLite's backup API), never the file the run writes. The places that name the defaults, all changed in one edit:\n   104\t\n   105\t| Place | What to change |\n     1\t\"\"\"06-views.md step 6: write one item's round into the views database. Themes before objects; a repeat adds a source;\n     2\ta `replace` decision is recorded as a revision (D202: the new piece revises the old, both stay in force) and is ordered by the day it\n     3\twas said (a later-arriving older statement is logged, not linked); a revised piece still linked elsewhere links the new piece there too; new views come with rungs, dependencies and\n     4\tsuccessions; a waiting dependency is resolved when the chain's year is created; the set of views whose reading\n     5\tchanged is returned for the re-judging round.\"\"\"\n     6\timport dataclasses\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport re\n     9\timport time\n    10\t\n    11\tfrom . import identity, store\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    15\tclass Written:\n    16\t    changed_views: set\n    17\t    new_views: dict            # candidate id -> view_id\n    18\t    evidence_ids: dict         # handover evidence id -> evidence_id\n    19\t    notes: list\n    20\t    links: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)      # D694: the reading links committed, with their final labels\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef _next_id(conn, table, column, prefix):\n    24\t    row = conn.execute(f'select {column} from {table} order by rowid desc limit 1').fetchone()\n    25\t    last = int(row[0][len(prefix):]) if row and row[0].startswith(prefix) and row[0][len(prefix):].isdigit() else 0\n    26\t    return f'{prefix}{last + 1}'\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tdef _store_piece(conn, e, seq, item):\n    30\t    evidence_id = _next_id(conn, 'evidence', 'evidence_id', 'e')\n    31\t    store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=e['quote'], one_line=e['one_line'], speaker=e['speaker'],\n    32\t                       original_who=e['original_who'], original_day=e['original_day'] or '', tier=e['tier'],   # D203: unknown stays unknown\n    33\t                       event_time=e['event_time'], seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'])\n    34\t    store.add_source(conn, evidence_id, item['input_id'], item['category'], item['publication_day'], e.get('location', ''), seq)\n    35\t    return evidence_id\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef _create_view(conn, c, object_id, object_kind, seq, item, universe):\n    39\t    view_id = _next_id(conn, 'views', 'view_id', 'v')\n    40\t    # the year is stored in its one canonical spelling so that a waiting dependency's year joins it (D163 plan, period text)\n    41\t    year = universe.canonical_year(object_id, c['year']) if hasattr(universe, 'canonical_year') else c['year']\n    42\t    store.create_view(conn, view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=c['kind'], looks_at=c['looks_at'],\n    43\t                      question=c['question'], due_day=c['due_day'], year=year, rungs=c['rungs'], seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'],\n    44\t                      created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n    45\t    if c.get('measure'):          # keyed candidates (extraction schema v4 and later) carry their key into the ledger\n    46\t        store.add_key(conn, view_id, c, seq)\n    47\t    return view_id\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef resolve_waiting(conn, new_view_id, seq, changed):\n    51\t    \"\"\"A new view on a chain satisfies dependencies waiting for its year on that chain.\"\"\"\n    52\t    v = store.view(conn, new_view_id)\n    53\t    chain = {new_view_id}\n    54\t    frontier = [new_view_id]\n    55\t    while frontier:\n    56\t        current = frontier.pop()\n    57\t        for row in conn.execute('select succeeds from successions where view_id=?', (current,)):\n    58\t            if row['succeeds'] not in chain:\n    59\t                chain.add(row['succeeds'])\n    60\t                frontier.append(row['succeeds'])\n    61\t    for dep in conn.execute('select * from dependencies where wait_year=? and wait_chain_view_id is not null', (v['year'],)):\n    62\t        if dep['wait_chain_view_id'] in chain:\n    63\t            already = conn.execute('select 1 from dependency_resolutions where dependency_id=?', (dep['dependency_id'],)).fetchone()\n    64\t            if not already and not store.would_cycle(conn, dep['view_id'], new_view_id):\n    65\t                store.insert(conn, 'dependency_resolutions', dependency_id=dep['dependency_id'], resolved_to=new_view_id, reason='created', seq=seq)\n    66\t                changed.add(dep['view_id'])\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef object_id_of(universe, candidate):\n    70\t    return universe.resolve(candidate['object']) or candidate['object']\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef oriented_like(c, previous, notes):\n    74\t    \"\"\"06-views: a successor's ladder keeps the predecessor's direction. A numeric ladder written the other way round (rung 1 the\n    75\t    lowest band where the predecessor's rung 1 is the highest) is the same ladder; it is stored reversed, rungs with their\n    76\t    labels and bounds, so positions mean the same along the chain. Undecidable pairs are stored as written.\"\"\"\n    77\t    from .matching import ladder_direction\n    78\t    before, after = (ladder_direction(previous) if previous else None), ladder_direction(c['rungs'])\n    79\t    if before is not None and after is not None and before != after:\n    80\t        notes.append(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: successor ladder reversed to the predecessor\\'s direction')\n    81\t        return dict(c, rungs=list(reversed(c['rungs'])))\n    82\t    return c\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tTIER_RANK = {'fact': 3, 'party_statement': 3, 'third_party_view': 2, 'rumour': 1}\n    86\tISO_DAY = re.compile(r'^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$')\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef revision_refused(incoming, old, new_day):\n    90\t    \"\"\"06-views, the Replace row, read since D202 as a revision: a later account of the same matter by a party entitled to give one (a\n    91\t    speaker revises its own guidance or forecast, an official confirms or denies a report, the original source revises). Returns the\n    92\t    reason the revision is refused, or '' when it may be recorded: the incoming piece needs a stated day, a tier at least the stored\n    93\t    piece's (a view never revises a fact or a party's statement), and, when it is a third-party view or a rumour, the same party as the\n    94\t    stored piece. Nothing is retired either way; a refused revision is stored as one more piece.\"\"\"\n    95\t    from .. import vocabulary\n    96\t    if not old:\n    97\t        return ''\n    98\t    if not ISO_DAY.match(new_day or ''):\n    99\t        return 'no stated day'\n   100\t    new_tier, old_tier = vocabulary.canonical('tier', incoming.get('tier')), vocabulary.canonical('tier', old.get('tier'))\n   101\t    if TIER_RANK.get(new_tier, 0) < TIER_RANK.get(old_tier, 0):\n   102\t        return f'{new_tier} cannot revise {old_tier}'\n   103\t    if new_tier in ('third_party_view', 'rumour') \\\n   104\t            and (incoming.get('original_who') or '').strip().casefold() != (old.get('original_who') or '').strip().casefold():\n   105\t        return f'another party\\'s {old_tier.replace(\"_\", \" \")}'       # an official confirms or denies; the original source revises\n   106\t    return ''\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tclass WriteConflict(ValueError):\n   110\t    \"\"\"The checked plan no longer fits the writable ledger; no partial write is retained.\"\"\"\n   163\t    progressed = conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 limit 1').fetchone() or \\\n   164\t        conn.execute('select 1 from days_completed limit 1').fetchone()\n   165\t    if progressed:\n   166\t        raise BaselineRefused('coverage start has passed in this ledger: the coverage-start reading runs only on a ledger that has processed nothing yet')\n   167\t    return 'run'\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\tdef run(conn, items_db, archive, cfg, *, ticker, coverage_start, transport=None, log=print):\n   171\t    \"\"\"Reads, checks and writes the starting figures; returns the step's record (or None when the configuration has no baseline setting or the step\n   172\t    ran before). All model calls first (archived, so a rerun after a failure reuses them), then every record, link and the step row in one commit.\"\"\"\n   173\t    setting = getattr(cfg, 'baseline', None)\n   174\t    if setting is None:\n   175\t        return None\n   176\t    system, task = prompt(setting.prompt_version)\n   177\t    if guard(conn, ticker, coverage_start) == 'skip':\n   178\t        log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: done before, skipped')\n   179\t        return None\n   180\t    items = report_items(items_db, ticker, coverage_start)\n   181\t    seq = store.next_sequence(conn)\n   182\t    at = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\n   183\t    if not items:\n   184\t        record = {'changed': [], 'report': [], 'kept': 0, 'refused': [], 'empty': [], 'note': f'no earnings report of {ticker} before {coverage_start}'}\n   185\t        store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, 'none'), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record), coverage_start, at)\n   186\t        conn.commit()\n   187\t        return record\n   188\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, {'publication_day': items[0]['publication_day'], 'category': 'T1', 'object_identifiers': [{'value': ticker}]}, [ticker])\n   189\t    readings = []\n   190\t    for view in sorted(shown, key=lambda v: int(v['view_id'][1:]) if v['view_id'][1:].isdigit() else 0):\n   191\t        lines = placement.question_lines([view])\n   192\t        for item in items:\n   193\t            answer = model.call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user_message(lines, item, task), SCHEMA, SCHEMA_NAME, STEP, transport=transport)\n   194\t            readings.append((view['view_id'], item, check_figures(answer.data.get('figures', []), item['text_page'])))\n   195\t    records, changed, refused, empty, kept = {}, [], [], [], 0\n   196\t    for view_id, item, figures in readings:\n   197\t        if not figures:\n   198\t            empty.append([view_id, item['input_id']])\n   199\t        for f in figures:\n   200\t            if not f['kept']:\n   201\t                refused.append({'view_id': view_id, 'input_id': item['input_id'], 'quote': f['quote'][:300], 'value': f['value'],\n   202\t                                'reason': 'quote not in the report' if not f['in_report'] else ('no label' if not f['labelled'] else 'value not printed in the quote')})\n   203\t                continue\n   204\t            key = (item['input_id'], comparable(f['quote']))\n   205\t            if key not in records:\n   206\t                evidence_id = _next_id(conn, 'evidence', 'evidence_id', 'e')\n   207\t                store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=f['quote'], one_line=one_line_of(f), speaker=item['publisher'],\n   208\t                                   original_who=item['publisher'], original_day=item['publication_day'], tier='fact', event_time='', seq=seq,\n   209\t                                   input_id=item['input_id'])\n   210\t                store.add_source(conn, evidence_id, item['input_id'], 'T1', item['publication_day'], '', seq)\n   211\t                records[key] = evidence_id\n   212\t            if store.link(conn, records[key], view_id, seq) and view_id not in changed:\n   213\t                changed.append(view_id)\n   214\t            kept += 1\n   215\t    record = {'changed': changed, 'report': [item['input_id'] for item in items], 'kept': kept, 'records': len(records), 'refused': refused, 'empty': empty}\n   216\t    store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, items[0]['publication_day']), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False), coverage_start, at)\n   217\t    conn.commit()\n   218\t    log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: {len(items)} report items, {len(readings)} readings, {len(records)} records linked to {changed}, '\n   219\t        f'{len(refused)} figures refused')\n   220\t    return record\n   115\t    missing = sorted(o for o in (aliases or {}) if o not in counts)\n   116\t    return (f'Objects with open views as of {as_of} (object, kind, number of views): {covered}.'\n   117\t            + (f' Objects in the universe with no view yet: {\", \".join(missing)}.' if missing else ''))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\tdef judged(ledger, view_id, as_of, detailed=False):\n   121\t    state = service.state_as_of(ledger, view_id, as_of)\n   122\t    if not state:\n   123\t        return None\n   124\t    rung = next((g for g in store.rungs_of(ledger, view_id) if g['position'] == state['position']), {})\n   125\t    result = {'position': state['position'], 'label': rung.get('label', '')}\n   126\t    if detailed:\n   127\t        result.update(condition=rung.get('condition', ''), day=state['judgement_day'], reasons=state['reasons'])\n   128\t    return result\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\tdef brief(ledger, results, as_of, detailed=False):\n   132\t    \"\"\"Candidate state at the requested date; analyst context is explicit and versioned by the caller.\"\"\"\n   133\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(ledger, as_of)\n   134\t    records = []\n   135\t    for result in results:\n   136\t        record = {'view_id': result['view_id'], 'object': result['object'], 'looks_at': result['looks_at'],\n   137\t                  'judged': judged(ledger, result['view_id'], as_of, detailed)}\n   138\t        if detailed:\n   139\t            record['question'] = result['question']\n   140\t        records.append(record)\n   141\t    return records\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\tdef related_views(ledger, view_ids, as_of, exclude=()):\n   145\t    \"\"\"The given views' neighbours in the ledger's dependency graph, as of the day: what each depends on (upstream)\n   146\t    and what depends on it (downstream), with the judged position; `exclude` are views already on the card.\n   215\t    return out[:limit]\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\tdef read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\n   219\t    \"\"\"The idea card: idea, what the idea's own search found, the reading (typed parts, the candidates each got, the\n   220\t    views each maps to, the summary, the claim), the related views from the dependency graph, the evaluation, every\n   221\t    view's bundle, the days, the trace of searches, and all call costs. No recorded view → no model call.\"\"\"\n   222\t    text = (text or '').strip()\n   223\t    if not text:\n   224\t        raise ValueError('an idea needs text')\n   225\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(ledger, as_of)\n   226\t    report = on_progress or (lambda stage: None)\n   227\t    report('search')\n   228\t    found = search.search(ledger, index, text, k, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed)\n   229\t    card = {'idea': {'text': text, 'as_of': as_of}, 'search': {'mode': found['mode'], 'candidates': [r['view_id'] for r in found['results'] or []]},\n   230\t            'reading': None, 'evaluation': None, 'related': [], 'views': [], 'days': bundle.days(ledger, as_of),\n   231\t            'no_recorded_view': found['results'] is None, 'cost': dict(NO_COST)}\n   232\t    if found['results'] is None:\n   233\t        return card\n   234\t    setting = cfg.idea\n   235\t    if setting is None:\n   236\t        raise config.ConfigError(f'config {cfg.version} has no idea setting')\n   237\t    decompose_prompt, map_prompt = prompts(setting)\n   238\t    started = time.time()\n   239\t    cost = dict(NO_COST)\n   240\t    cost['cached'] = True\n   241\t\n   242\t    def spend(answer):\n   243\t        cost['usd'] += answer.cost_usd\n   244\t        cost['input_tokens'] += answer.input_tokens\n   245\t        cost['output_tokens'] += answer.output_tokens\n   246\t        cost['turns'] += 1\n   247\t        cost['cached'] = cost['cached'] and answer.cached\n   248\t\n   249\t    # call 1: the parts\n   250\t    report('decompose')\n   251\t    user = f'Idea: {text}\\nDay: {as_of} (the library as judged on this day)\\n\\n{object_list(ledger, as_of, aliases)}'\n   252\t    made, slips = call_english(archive, cfg, setting, decompose_prompt, user, DECOMPOSE, 'idea_decompose', transport,\n   253\t                               lambda d: [f for p in d['parts'] for f in (p['looks_for'], p['period'])])\n   254\t    for answer in made:\n   255\t        spend(answer)\n   256\t    first = made[-1]\n   257\t    parts = [dict(p) for p in first.data['parts'][:MAX_PARTS]]\n   258\t    # the service: one search per part, the candidates each part got\n   259\t    report('retrieve')\n   260\t    detailed = setting.prompt_version == 'idea-v12'\n   261\t    idea_rows = brief(ledger, found['results'][:IDEA_ROWS], as_of, detailed)\n   262\t    trace, candidates, ranks = [], [], []\n   263\t    queries = [((part.get('query') or '').strip() or canonical_query(part, aliases), canonical_query(part, aliases)) for part in parts]\n   264\t    if semantic and found['mode'] == 'semantic':\n   265\t        search.warm_queries(index, [q for pair in queries for q in pair], embed)      # one embeddings round trip for every part instead of two per part\n   266\t    # a part's candidates: the service's canonical query and the model's own, interleaved (tried 2026-10-25 and dropped:\n   267\t    # the object's views ranked by the idea text alone lost the model's finds, gold direct right 17 → 15 of 19)\n   268\t    for i, (part, (query, own)) in enumerate(zip(parts, queries)):\n   269\t        hit = search.search(ledger, index, query, PER_PART, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed)\n   270\t        steady = search.search(ledger, index, own, PER_PART, as_of, aliases=aliases, semantic=semantic, embed=embed) if own.lower() != query.lower() else hit\n   271\t        rows = brief(ledger, merged(steady['results'] or [], hit['results'] or [], PER_PART), as_of, detailed)\n   272\t        candidates.append(rows)\n   273\t        ranks.append({r['view_id']: n for n, r in enumerate(hit['results'] or [])})      # the part's own search order, the tie-break among the model's direct views\n   274\t        trace.append({'tool': 'search', 'part': i, 'query': query, 'canonical': own, 'returned': [r['view_id'] for r in rows]})\n   275\t    # call 2: the mapping\n   276\t    report('map')\n   277\t    map_schema, payload = CONTRACTS.get(setting.prompt_version, (MAP, full_payload))\n   278\t    user = payload(text, as_of, parts, candidates, idea_rows)\n   279\t    made, more = call_english(archive, cfg, setting, map_prompt, user, map_schema, 'idea_map', transport,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
