nks LG Innotek to NVIDIA’s physical AI ')\n('truenorth:story:story_01a163d0-31d0-7421-8e06-4081a45c69ea', 'markets.businessinsider.com', 'Zadara Achieves NVIDIA AI Cloud Ready Validation', 'Oct. 22, 2026, 08:02 AM\\nIrvine, Calif., Oct. 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Zadara , a leading provider of sovereign AI cloud infrastructure, today announced it has achieved NVIDIA AI Cloud Ready ISV Initiative validated partner status, part of the NVIDIA Cloud Partner (NCP) program. Zadara will mark ')\n('truenorth:story:story_01a16422-8522-7fc1-8724-874e96196cc4', 'newswire.ca', 'Rockwell Automation Adds Support for NVIDIA Nemotron Models', \"Rockwell Automation, Inc.\\nManufacturers gain additional deployment flexibility for industrial AI orchestration through support for NVIDIA Nemotron models\\nMILWAUKEE , Oct. 22, 2026 /CNW/ -- Rockwell Automation, Inc. (NYSE: ROK), the world's largest company dedicated to industrial automation and digit\")\n('truenorth:story:story_01a16851-902e-7540-b254-7fcf3e9992b4', 'datacentremagazine.com', 'Vertiv and NVIDIA Launch New AI Factory Deployment Approach', 'GTC: How Vertiv and NVIDIA Halve AI Factory Deployment Time\\nBy Saffron Humphreys\\nVertiv and NVIDIA have launched a new AI factory deployment approach at NVIDIA GTC Berlin.\\nThe model cuts infrastructure deployment time from approximately 90 days to 45 days, up to 50% faster, by shifting more assembly')\n('truenorth:story:story_01a17327-aeda-7362-b65e-a4680d120bbd', 'technews.tw', 'Supermicro and Nokia Deploy NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer Solutions for AI-RAN', 'Supermicro and Nokia Deploy NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer Solutions for AI-RAN\\n[provider summary, not the article]\\nSupermicro and Nokia are deploying NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer solutions for AI-RAN workloads at the network edge. Supermicro says its servers for NVIDIA ARC are now available; some describ')\n('truenorth:story:story_01a177c4-aed3-7d01-b3d7-63d36293229a', 'prnewswire.com', 'SWI Compute Launches to Build NVIDIA AI Factories', 'SWI Compute Emerges from Stealth to Turn Gigawatts of Power Into NVIDIA AI Factories, Starting in Europe\\nSINGAPORE and AMSTERDAM , Oct. 26, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- SWI Compute today emerged from stealth to build and operate NVIDIA AI factories, launching first in Europe. The global AI infrastructure co')\n('truenorth:story:story_01a178bc-293b-7301-baac-5776ecf91e91', 'morningstar.com', 'NVIDIA Expresses Interest in Meta Platforms Equity Offering', 'Nvidia, AMD and Broadcom could buy Meta shares as part of $35 billion stock offering\\nBy Britney Nguyen\\nMeta is looking to raise a total of $95 billion through stock-related deals that stretch into early next year\\nMeta announced a $35 billion equity offering on Monday.\\nMeta Platforms intends to raise')\n('extra:b23f73a08a535993119430f5', 'cnbc.com', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room\\nBrands\\nVersant Media\\nMS NOW\\nUSA Network\\nSYFY\\nRotten Tomatoes\\nUSA Sports\\nOxygen True Crime\\nE!\\nFandango\\nFreeTV\\nGolf Channel\\nGolfPass\\nGolfNow\\nFull Swing\\nLogin\\nRegister\\nLOADING...\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\nMore\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\nLOADING...\\nCNBC Transcript: Nvi')\n('extra:1d912c1e5fc3a34f3c5bc52a', 'cnbc.com', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room', 'Brands\\nVersant Media\\nMS NOW\\nUSA Network\\nSYFY\\nRotten Tomatoes\\nUSA Sports\\nOxygen True Crime\\nE!\\nFandango\\nFreeTV\\nGolf Channel\\nGolfPass\\nGolfNow\\nFull Swing\\nLogin\\nRegister\\nLOADING...\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\nMore\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\nLOADING...\\nCNBC | VERSANT Press Room\\nCNBC Excerpts: Nvidi')\n('extra:ea981681c9e20cb5e31f7126', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face | NVIDIA Blog', 'I’m excited to announce that NVIDIA has agreed to acquire Hugging Face for $12,930,300,000. Together, we will scale Hugging Face’s platform, strengthen its infrastructure and expand access to AI for developers and institutions worldwide.\\nOver the past decade, Clem, Julien, Thomas and the team at Hug')\n('extra:ed34d148788e5d6f51faf5b5', 'blogs.nvidia.com', '‘Now We Can Know Everything and Do Anything,’ Jensen Huang Says at Dreamforce | NVIDIA Blog', 'At Dreamforce, Salesforce and NVIDIA announced Koa, a CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, post-trained from Nemotron on 27 years of Salesforce CRM intelligence — and running entirely within Salesforce’s own infrastructure.\\nThat was the message NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang brought to Salesforc')\n('extra:e85b9e2ad448ed75ecf99831', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA, Microsoft Kick Off a New Beginning for Windows PCs with RTX Spark and AI Agents | NVIDIA Blog', 'RTX Spark preorders open today alongside a preview of NVIDIA DGX Station for Windows, the first deskside AI supercomputer built for the Windows enterprise desktop.\\nAt a Microsoft event in San Francisco on Wednesday, NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang and Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella outlined how NVI')\n('extra:494a9fa3bb713759384d4568', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'Germany Wants to Lead the World in Industrial AI: How NVIDIA Will Help | NVIDIA Blog', 'German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang discussed how to merge traditional German engineering with state-of-the-art AI.\\nIn the cavernous hall of Kraftwerk, a former power station in Berlin, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang sat ')\n('extra:99d146f2162c85d645ba0fbd', 'investor.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms\\nNVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms\\nAugust 31, 2026\\nCompanies Expand Collaboration Across Multigenerational Cloud AI ')\n('extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108', 'investor.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027\\nNVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027\\nAugust 26, 2026\\nRevenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago\\nData Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\\nSANTA CLARA, Calif.')\nv5 NVIDIA expects total revenue to grow approximately 70% in FY2028, with supply constraining growth. We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028. This is a supply-constrained outlook.\nv8 NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 18% sequentially. Q2 data center revenue increased 18% quarter-over-quarter to $89 billion with strong contributions from both sub segments hyperscale and ACIE, which includes our NeoCloud, industrial and enterprise customers.\nv8 NVIDIA hyperscale revenue was $49 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 13% sequentially, driven by Blackwell. Hyperscale revenue of $49 billion grew 13% sequentially, driven by sustained strength in Blackwell\nv6,v7 NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeds $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler CapEx is expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027. With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\nv3,v4,v5,v8 AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs, along with Vera CPUs, from Q2 FY2027 through Q2 FY2029. AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\nv4,v5,v8 AWS plans to serve NVIDIA’s Nemotron open-model family on Amazon Bedrock and SageMaker. AWS will serve NVIDIA Nemotron family of open models on Amazon Bedrock and SageMaker.\nv8 e2295 Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year. Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth. {'input_id': 'gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258', 'title': 'Going Into Earnings, Is Nvidia Stock a Buy, a Sell, or Fairly Valued?', 'source_uri': 'https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/going-into-earnings-is-nvidia-stock-buy-sell-or-fairly-valued-8'}\nv8 e5309 NVIDIA reported $164 billion of Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027. The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027. {'input_id': 'gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca', 'title': 'Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most', 'source_uri': 'https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/18/global-ai-infrastructure-spending-will-hit-usd31-6-trillion-by-2050-this-is-the-stock-that-could-benefit-the-most/'}\nv4,v8 e5384 Nscale signed a six-year agreement in August 2026 for Anthropic to lease capacity at Nscale’s West Virginia data center, valued at up to $45 billion. Last month, Nscale signed a landmark agreement with Anthropic to lease capacity at its flagship data center in West Virginia. The six-year deal is valued at up to $45 billion. {'input_id': 'gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db', 'title': 'NVIDIA-backed \"British Oracle\" Races for U.S. IPO with $35 Billion Valuation Target', 'source_uri': 'https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/76493332/nvidia-backed-british-oracle-races-for-us-ipo-with-35'}\nv4,v8 e5385 Nscale estimated that its West Virginia data center, including a 2 GW gas-fired power plant, would cost about $70 billion and begin phased commissioning by the end of 2027. Nscale estimates that this data center, currently under construction, is expected to begin phased commissioning by the end of next year, with a total cost of approximately US$70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant to support its operations. {'input_id': 'gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db', 'title': 'NVIDIA-backed \"British Oracle\" Races for U.S. IPO with $35 Billion Valuation Target', 'source_uri': 'https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/76493332/nvidia-backed-british-oracle-races-for-us-ipo-with-35'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data\\\")\nbase=root/\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\"\ndef conn(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ninputs=[(f\\\"old-{i}\\\",base/f\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\",base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\"served\\\",root/\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\",root/\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")]\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\n c=conn(p); rows=list(c.execute(\\\"select e.evidence_id,one_line,quote,group_concat(view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) group by e.evidence_id\\\"))\n pat=r\\\"(implying|implies|annualiz|annualis|implied|on track|at that (rate|pace)|run.rate|extrapolat|would (yield|put|imply)|equates to|equivalent to)\\\"\n hits=[(id,v,l,q) for id,l,q,v in rows if re.search(pat,l or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I) and not re.search(pat,q or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I)]\n print(name,len(hits))\n for id,v,l,q in hits[:8]: print(id,v,l,\\\"|\\\",q)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data\\\")\nbase=root/\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\"\ndef conn(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ninputs=[(f\\\"old-{i}\\\",base/f\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\",base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\"served\\\",root/\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\",root/\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")]\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\n c=conn(p); rows=list(c.execute(\\\"select e.evidence_id,one_line,quote,group_concat(view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) group by e.evidence_id\\\"))\n pat=r\\\"(implying|implies|annualiz|annualis|implied|on track|at that (rate|pace)|run.rate|extrapolat|would (yield|put|imply)|equates to|equivalent to)\\\"\n hits=[(id,v,l,q) for id,l,q,v in rows if re.search(pat,l or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I) and not re.search(pat,q or '\\\\'''\\\\'',re.I)]\n print(name,len(hits))\n for id,v,l,q in hits[:8]: print(id,v,l,\\\"|\\\",q)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 32\ne1265 v4 NVIDIA guided to $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter, implying 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\ne1706 v6,v7 Jensen Huang said recent AI spending is only the beginning, implying further substantial AI spending over the coming years. | He's looking years into the future and declaring that the recent, massive spending on AI is just the tip of the iceberg.\ne2294 v4,v5 Morningstar sees upside in NVIDIA shares conditional on the company staying on track to meet its near- and medium-term revenue targets. | We still see upside in Nvidia stock as long as it remains on pace to hit its near- and medium-term revenue targets.\ne2934 v4 Analysts’ consensus estimate for NVIDIA FY2027 Q2 revenue was $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% growth. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\ne3161 v5 The author calculates that $425 billion of FY2027 revenue combined with 70% FY2028 growth would imply more than $700 billion of FY2028 revenue. | If Nvidia reaches $425 billion in revenue this year, that would mean over $700 billion in revenue next fiscal year and knocking on the door of $1 trillion a few years from now.\ne3168 v35 thenewstack.io calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price was roughly 86 times Hugging Face’s estimated annualized revenue. | Against a $12.9 billion price tag, that’s a multiple of roughly 86.\ne3301 v35 Reuters, citing The Information, reported on August 27 that NVIDIA had agreed to acquire Hugging Face for a price implying roughly 86 times sales. | On August 27, Reuters reported that Nvidia had agreed to acquire Hugging Face, citing The Information. The arithmetic is obscene at roughly 86 times sales.\ne3346 v4 Nvidia guided third-quarter revenue to $105.84 billion–$110.16 billion, implying 85.7%–93.2% year-over-year growth from $57.01 billion. | For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\nold-2 19\ne1464 v14 The Register, citing Orbital CEO, said orbital data centers would require Starship to reach Musk's stated $10-per-kilogram launch-cost goal, which would put the estimated cost to orbit for the AI1 at about $33,300. | For orbital datacenters to be cost-effective, Starship is going to need to get the cost per kilogram down to Elon’s stated goal of $10, Ortibal CEO told El Reg earlier this year. That would bring the cost to orbit to about $33,300\ne2151 v14,v21 Daniel Sparks calculated that NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue guidance midpoint implies about $9 billion of sequential growth, or 11%, versus roughly $13.5 billion and 20% sequential growth in the first quarter. | The midpoint asks for about $9 billion of new revenue versus the first quarter, which had itself added about $13.5 billion versus the one before it. In growth terms, that's a step down to about 11% sequentially from 20%.\ne2772 v14,v21 Analysts’ consensus revenue estimate is $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% sales growth for the period being discussed. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\ne2870 v9 NVIDIA indicated it could satisfy around 70% of current demand, implying the company was unable to meet the remainder. | Nvidia also indicated that it can currently satisfy only around 70% of demand.\ne2911 v17 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand implies revenue growth above 70% for FY2028, but product supply constrains how much the company can supply. | CEO Jensen Huang said demand \"is much greater than 70%,\" but the company is constrained on the amount of product it can supply.\ne2997 v34 Thenewstack.io calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price is about 86 times Hugging Face's reported annualized revenue. | Against a $12.9 billion price tag, that’s a multiple of roughly 86.\ne3169 v14 NVIDIA guided third-quarter revenue to $105.84 billion–$110.16 billion, implying year-over-year growth of 85.7%–93.2% from $57.01 billion. | For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\ne3198 v34 Futurum calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price equates to 86–129 times Hugging Face’s estimated $100–150 million annual recurring revenue as of mid-2026. | Against that range, the reported $12.9 billion price works out to somewhere between 86x and 129x revenue, a multiple that only makes sense if NVIDIA were to be paying for future distribution leverage and developer mindshare rather than current financial performance.\nold-3 22\ne1260 v3 NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91 billion for FY2027 Q2, which the author said implied 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\ne2334 v3 Daniel Sparks calculated that NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue guidance midpoint implied about $9 billion of sequential revenue growth, or approximately 11%, versus about $13.5 billion and 20% sequential growth in the first quarter. | The midpoint asks for about $9 billion of new revenue versus the first quarter, which had itself added about $13.5 billion versus the one before it. In growth terms, that's a step down to about 11% sequentially from 20%.\ne2384 v3 NVIDIA disclosed a stake in SpaceX worth nearly $21 billion, equivalent to roughly 122.8 million shares, last week. | Just last week, Nvidia disclosed a stake of nearly $21 billion – roughly 122.8 million shares at $170.86 per share – in SpaceX, the Elon Musk-led space and AI company.\ne3153 v4 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand implies revenue growth greater than 70%, while product supply constrains the company. | CEO Jensen Huang said demand \"is much greater than 70%,\" but the company is constrained on the amount of product it can supply.\ne3220 v3,v4 The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue of $425 billion in FY2027 would imply revenue above $700 billion in FY2028. | If Nvidia reaches $425 billion in revenue this year, that would mean over $700 billion in revenue next fiscal year\ne3224 v4,v38 The author calculated that $700 billion of FY2028 revenue at a 64% operating margin would imply $448 billion in operating earnings. | Assuming Nvidia can reach $700 billion in revenue in fiscal year 2028, a 64% operating margin would equate to $448 billion in operating earnings\ne3370 v4 NVIDIA’s outlook, as described by the author, implies roughly 70% revenue growth in FY2028 and is supply-constrained. | Next year's top-line growth is pegged at roughly 70%, and that is the scenario where supply runs out.\ne3588 v39 The author calculated that NVIDIA's reported $12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition price equals about 86 times Hugging Face's annualised sales. | Nvidia would therefore be paying about 86 times sales—a multiple that looks absurd if Hugging Face is treated as an ordinary software company.\nserved 15\ne1314 v2,v10,v21 NVIDIA said it is targeting capacity requiring 2 gigawatts of power; the report characterized the implied buildout as involving hundreds of thousands of GPUs. | Nvidia said it's targeting enough capacity to require 2 gigawatts of power, which indicates a massive buildout with hundreds of thousands of graphics processing units.\ne1391 v6 The article reported average GDDR6/GDDR7 module prices up $19–$20, implying about $75 higher cost for an 8 GB graphics card and about $100 after China's 13% VAT. | Currently, the DRAM prices for GDDR6 and GDDR7 modules have risen by an average of $19-$20. This means that an 8 GB graphics card will see a price hike of around $75 US, and since China has a VAT of 13%, when you factor it all in, the price difference jumps to $100 US.\ne1534 v2,v10 NVIDIA guided to $91 billion of revenue for the current quarter, implying 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\ne1833 v2,v10 Microsoft said its AI business exceeded $37 billion in annualized revenue, up 123%, and commercial remaining performance obligations were $627 billion. | Microsoft ( NASDAQ:MSFT ) told investors on its most recent call that its “AI business surpassed $37 billion ARR, up 123%”, with commercial remaining performance obligations, its committed backlog, at $627 billion.\ne3051 v2,v10,v13 Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA Q2 FY2027 revenue of about $92.1 billion and EPS of $2.09, implying 97% revenue growth and nearly doubled profits year over year. | Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia to post roughly $92.1 billion in revenue and earnings per share (EPS) of $2.09 for the second quarter. That would amount to 97% revenue growth and nearly a doubling of profits year over year.\ne3519 v2 The Kobeissi Letter estimated conditionally that NVIDIA delivering its $108 billion Q3 guidance would imply roughly 1,730% revenue growth over four years. | If Nvidia delivers on its $108 billion third-quarter guidance, the company would have grown revenue by roughly 1,730% in just four years\ne3587 v2,v10 The author reports analysts’ consensus revenue estimate of $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% growth. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\ne3598 v2,v10 NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q3 revenue to $108 billion, implying 89% year-over-year growth. | Its Q3 outlook calls for revenue of $108 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 89%.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data\\\")\nbase=root/\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\"\ndef conn(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ninputs=[(f\\\"old-{i}\\\",base/f\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\",base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\"served\\\",root/\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\",root/\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")]\ndef amounts(t):\n return set(re.findall(r\\\"(?:\\\\\"'$|USD'\"\\\\s*)([\\\\d,]+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)\\\\s*(?:[mbt]\\\\b|million|billion|trillion)\\\",t or \\\"\\\",re.I))\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\n c=conn(p); i=conn(ip); out=[]\n cache={}\n for eid,one,q,s in c.execute(\\\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote,created_from_input from evidence\\\"):\n  if not amounts(one)-amounts(q) or not re.search(r\\\"expect|forecast|guidance|impli|project|estim|will|would|equiv|annualiz|annualis\\\",one,re.I):continue\n  if s not in cache:\n   r=i.execute(\\\"select title,text,text_article,text_page from items where input_id=?\\\",(s,)).fetchone()\n   cache[s]=\\\" \\\".join(t or \\\"\\\" for t in r).replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\").lower() if r else \\\"\\\"\n  miss=[a for a in amounts(one)-amounts(q) if not re.search(r\\\"(?<\"'!['\"\\\\d.])\\\"+re.escape(a.replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\"))+r\\\"(?\"'!'\"\\\\d)\\\",cache[s])]\n  if miss: out.append((eid,miss,one,q))\n print(name,len(out))\n for r in out[:15]: print(*r,sep=\\\" | \\\")\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data\\\")\nbase=root/\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\"\ndef conn(p):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ninputs=[(f\\\"old-{i}\\\",base/f\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\",base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\"served\\\",root/\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\",root/\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")]\ndef amounts(t):\n return set(re.findall(r\\\"(?:\\\\\"'$|USD'\"\\\\s*)([\\\\d,]+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)\\\\s*(?:[mbt]\\\\b|million|billion|trillion)\\\",t or \\\"\\\",re.I))\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\n c=conn(p); i=conn(ip); out=[]\n cache={}\n for eid,one,q,s in c.execute(\\\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote,created_from_input from evidence\\\"):\n  if not amounts(one)-amounts(q) or not re.search(r\\\"expect|forecast|guidance|impli|project|estim|will|would|equiv|annualiz|annualis\\\",one,re.I):continue\n  if s not in cache:\n   r=i.execute(\\\"select title,text,text_article,text_page from items where input_id=?\\\",(s,)).fetchone()\n   cache[s]=\\\" \\\".join(t or \\\"\\\" for t in r).replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\").lower() if r else \\\"\\\"\n  miss=[a for a in amounts(one)-amounts(q) if not re.search(r\\\"(?<\"'!['\"\\\\d.])\\\"+re.escape(a.replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\"))+r\\\"(?\"'!'\"\\\\d)\\\",cache[s])]\n  if miss: out.append((eid,miss,one,q))\n print(name,len(out))\n for r in out[:15]: print(*r,sep=\\\" | \\\")\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 5\ne724 | ['1.71'] | Precedence Research valued the global GPU market at $101.54 billion in 2025 and projected it to reach about $1.71 trillion by 2035, a 32.62% CAGR over 2026–2035. | The global graphics processing unit (GPU) market was valued at USD 101.54 billion in 2025 and is projected to grow from USD 136.06 billion in 2026 to approximately USD 1,712.56 billion by 2035, registering a CAGR of 32.62% during the forecast period from 2026 to 2035.\ne1226 | ['9'] | Brookfield signed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to $9 billion in project funding for the NAVER AI factory expansion. | Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\ne1227 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned investment in NAVER is conditional on NAVER securing at least $9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\ne3238 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\ne3296 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue to exceed $40 billion in FY2028, more than double its FY2027 expectation. | and more than double that the year after.\nold-2 6\ne1056 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned NAVER investment is conditional on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion of binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\ne1057 | ['9'] | Brookfield executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to US$9 billion in project funding for the GAK Sejong expansion. | Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\ne3073 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\ne3127 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | That growth feeds Nvidia's newest business line, standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\ne3877 | ['3'] | NVIDIA was reported to be expected to provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s proposed $5 billion to $6 billion fundraising, or roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\ne4988 | ['1.5'] | Brad Gerstner said annual AI-infrastructure capital spending could reach $1.5 trillion and would require customers to pay for the capacity. | \"If you're going to build a trillion and a half dollars a year in capex, somebody has to pay for it,\" he said.\nold-3 5\ne1221 | ['9'] | Brookfield executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to US$9 billion in project funding for the NAVER AI factory. | On the other side, Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\ne1222 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned direct investment in NAVER depends on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\ne3302 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\ne3356 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue to be $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\ne4125 | ['3'] | The author estimates NVIDIA will provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s planned $5 billion to $6 billion funding round, or about $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\nserved 5\ne1490 | ['9'] | The article says NVIDIA's planned investment is conditional on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\ne2114 | ['1'] | SiliconANGLE reported on 2026-08-10 that Google, Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, SpaceX, OpenAI and Anthropic had collectively spent more than $1 trillion on AI projects and infrastructure over the preceding three years, and were expected to invest more. | Collectively, these companies have spent more than a trillion dollars on AI projects and infrastructure in the last three years, and they’re expected to invest even more in future.\ne2882 | ['5.0', '4.0'] | The Futurum Group estimated Helios system cost at $5.0 million–$5.5 million versus $3.5 million–$4.0 million for NVIDIA Vera Rubin; the estimate’s period is unspecified. | Helios also reportedly costs more per system than Nvidia's Vera Rubin, an estimated $5 million to $5.5 million versus $3.5 million to $4 million, according to the Futurum Group, a premium that needs to be justified by performance.\ne3936 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\ne3997 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
