65\\\").fetchone()))\n print(name,c.execute(\\\"select max(day) from days_completed\\\").fetchone()[0], \\\"first views tied\\\",list(map(tuple,c.execute(\\\"select created_seq,group_concat(view_id) from views group by created_seq having count(*)>1 limit 2\\\"))))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 e3238 v15 NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\nold-1 e3296 v5 NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue to exceed $40 billion in FY2028, more than double its FY2027 expectation. | and more than double that the year after.\n(1, 'Strongly bullish', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $400 billion.', 16)\n(2, 'Bullish', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion.', 7)\n(3, 'Neutral', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $300 billion and less than $350 billion.', 7)\n(4, 'Bearish', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $300 billion.', 7)\n(5, 'Strongly bearish', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is less than $250 billion.', 16)\nj865 {'view_id': 'v10', 'seq': 1204, 'why_changed': 'The rung remains 1 and no new transaction terms are shown. The updated AI-capex themes now put 2026 hyperscaler data-center capex at rung 4 and 2027 capex at rung 4, strengthening the contextual support for Firmus financing and changing the supporting outlook, without changing the implied completion date.', 'reference': 'No market consensus is supplied; the status-quo reference is no completion by December 31, 2026 (rung 2).', 'implied_outcome': 'Completion of the indicated approximately US$500 million preference-share investment by December 31, 2026 is more likely than non-completion. The report ties the preference shares to conversion at Firmus’ IPO later in 2026, placing the intended transaction before the deadline, though it does not confirm that NVIDIA has committed.'}\nold-1 2026-09-20 first views tied [(22, 'v3,v4,v5'), (42, 'v6,v7')]\nold-2 e3073 v8,v16 NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\nold-2 e3127 v8 NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | That growth feeds Nvidia's newest business line, standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\nold-2 e3877 v38 NVIDIA was reported to be expected to provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s proposed $5 billion to $6 billion fundraising, or roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\ngnews:21017fa01f34cb308af3b38b Nvidia Is Eyeing a $2.5 Billion Bet on Mira Murati's AI Startup gurufocus.com ['Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital. The potential deal would deepen an already close relationship.']\nold-2 2026-09-20 first views tied [(8, 'v2,v3'), (42, 'v5,v6')]\nold-3 e3302 v14,v30 NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\nold-3 e3356 v14,v30 NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue to be $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\nold-3 e4125 v33 The author estimates NVIDIA will provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s planned $5 billion to $6 billion funding round, or about $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\nold-3 2026-09-20 first views tied [(22, 'v3,v4,v5'), (42, 'v6,v7')]\nserved e3936 v7,v24 NVIDIA projected $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\nserved e3997 v7 NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\nserved 2026-08-28 first views tied [(42, 'v4,v5'), (1143, 'v66,v67')]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
