{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/extraction.py | sed -n '642,704p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/baseline.py | sed -n '163,218p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '91,111p;169,184p'\"","aggregated_output":"   642\t                dropped.append((c['id'], f'candidate admission: {problem}'))\n   643\t                continue\n   644\t        if c.get('measure'):          # keyed candidates keep their actual scope; reference lists do not gate admission (D155)\n   645\t            problem = check_bounds(c['rungs'])\n   646\t            if problem:\n   647\t                dropped.append((c['id'], f'candidate ladder bounds: {problem}'))\n   648\t                continue\n   649\t            if universe is not None:\n   650\t                object_id = universe.resolve(c['object']) or c['object']\n   651\t                scope, source = universe.scope_and_source(object_id, c['measure'], c.get('scope', ''), c.get('event_type', 'n/a'))\n   652\t                c = dict(c, object=object_id, scope=scope, scope_source=source, key_version=2)\n   653\t                if c['measure'] not in ('event', 'policy_event'):\n   654\t                    period = universe.fiscal_period(object_id, c.get('year', ''), bare_is_calendar=True)                             # and the period of a yearly number\n   655\t                    if period:\n   656\t                        c = dict(c, period_start=period[0], period_end=period[1])\n   657\t            try:\n   658\t                start = datetime.date.fromisoformat(c['period_start'])\n   659\t                end = datetime.date.fromisoformat(c['period_end'])\n   660\t                if start > end:\n   661\t                    raise ValueError('start after end')\n   662\t            except (KeyError, ValueError):\n   663\t                dropped.append((c['id'], 'invalid period: expected real dates with start <= end'))\n   664\t                continue\n   665\t        candidates.append(c)\n   666\t        candidate_ids.add(c['id'])\n   667\t    evidence = []\n   668\t    kept_ids = set()\n   669\t    by_quote = {}\n   670\t    alias = {}\n   671\t    for e in data.get('evidence', []):\n   672\t        quote = normalise(e['quote'])\n   673\t        if len(quote) < 8 or quote not in body:\n   674\t            subject_names = [universe.companies[o['value']]['name'] for o in item.get('object_identifiers') or []\n   675\t                             if universe is not None and o['value'] in getattr(universe, 'companies', {})]\n   676\t            repaired = repair_quote(e['quote'], text, subject_names)\n   677\t            if repaired is None or normalise(repaired) not in body:\n   678\t                dropped.append((e['id'], 'quote not in item'))\n   679\t                continue\n   680\t            e = dict(e, quote=repaired)\n   681\t            quote = normalise(repaired)\n   682\t        links = [l for l in e['links'] if l in shown_ids or l in candidate_ids]\n   683\t        if quote in by_quote:            # the same sentence read out twice is one piece with both links\n   684\t            first = by_quote[quote]\n   685\t            first['links'].extend(l for l in links if l not in first['links'])\n   686\t            alias[e['id']] = first['id']\n   687\t            dropped.append((e['id'], f'same quote as {first[\"id\"]}; merged'))\n   688\t            continue\n   689\t        e = dict(e, links=links, original_day=statement_day(e.get('original_day')))\n   690\t        by_quote[quote] = e\n   691\t        evidence.append(e)\n   692\t        kept_ids.add(e['id'])\n   693\t    final_candidates = candidates_with_evidence(candidates, kept_ids, item, dropped, alias)\n   694\t    for e in evidence:\n   695\t        e['links'] = [l for l in e['links'] if l in shown_ids or any(c['id'] == l for c in final_candidates)]\n   696\t    return evidence, final_candidates, dropped\n   163\t    progressed = conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 limit 1').fetchone() or \\\n   164\t        conn.execute('select 1 from days_completed limit 1').fetchone()\n   165\t    if progressed:\n   166\t        raise BaselineRefused('coverage start has passed in this ledger: the coverage-start reading runs only on a ledger that has processed nothing yet')\n   167\t    return 'run'\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\tdef run(conn, items_db, archive, cfg, *, ticker, coverage_start, transport=None, log=print):\n   171\t    \"\"\"Reads, checks and writes the starting figures; returns the step's record (or None when the configuration has no baseline setting or the step\n   172\t    ran before). All model calls first (archived, so a rerun after a failure reuses them), then every record, link and the step row in one commit.\"\"\"\n   173\t    setting = getattr(cfg, 'baseline', None)\n   174\t    if setting is None:\n   175\t        return None\n   176\t    system, task = prompt(setting.prompt_version)\n   177\t    if guard(conn, ticker, coverage_start) == 'skip':\n   178\t        log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: done before, skipped')\n   179\t        return None\n   180\t    items = report_items(items_db, ticker, coverage_start)\n   181\t    seq = store.next_sequence(conn)\n   182\t    at = time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\n   183\t    if not items:\n   184\t        record = {'changed': [], 'report': [], 'kept': 0, 'refused': [], 'empty': [], 'note': f'no earnings report of {ticker} before {coverage_start}'}\n   185\t        store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, 'none'), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record), coverage_start, at)\n   186\t        conn.commit()\n   187\t        return record\n   188\t    shown = extraction.shown_views(conn, cfg, {'publication_day': items[0]['publication_day'], 'category': 'T1', 'object_identifiers': [{'value': ticker}]}, [ticker])\n   189\t    readings = []\n   190\t    for view in sorted(shown, key=lambda v: int(v['view_id'][1:]) if v['view_id'][1:].isdigit() else 0):\n   191\t        lines = placement.question_lines([view])\n   192\t        for item in items:\n   193\t            answer = model.call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user_message(lines, item, task), SCHEMA, SCHEMA_NAME, STEP, transport=transport)\n   194\t            readings.append((view['view_id'], item, check_figures(answer.data.get('figures', []), item['text_page'])))\n   195\t    records, changed, refused, empty, kept = {}, [], [], [], 0\n   196\t    for view_id, item, figures in readings:\n   197\t        if not figures:\n   198\t            empty.append([view_id, item['input_id']])\n   199\t        for f in figures:\n   200\t            if not f['kept']:\n   201\t                refused.append({'view_id': view_id, 'input_id': item['input_id'], 'quote': f['quote'][:300], 'value': f['value'],\n   202\t                                'reason': 'quote not in the report' if not f['in_report'] else ('no label' if not f['labelled'] else 'value not printed in the quote')})\n   203\t                continue\n   204\t            key = (item['input_id'], comparable(f['quote']))\n   205\t            if key not in records:\n   206\t                evidence_id = _next_id(conn, 'evidence', 'evidence_id', 'e')\n   207\t                store.add_evidence(conn, evidence_id=evidence_id, quote=f['quote'], one_line=one_line_of(f), speaker=item['publisher'],\n   208\t                                   original_who=item['publisher'], original_day=item['publication_day'], tier='fact', event_time='', seq=seq,\n   209\t                                   input_id=item['input_id'])\n   210\t                store.add_source(conn, evidence_id, item['input_id'], 'T1', item['publication_day'], '', seq)\n   211\t                records[key] = evidence_id\n   212\t            if store.link(conn, records[key], view_id, seq) and view_id not in changed:\n   213\t                changed.append(view_id)\n   214\t            kept += 1\n   215\t    record = {'changed': changed, 'report': [item['input_id'] for item in items], 'kept': kept, 'records': len(records), 'refused': refused, 'empty': empty}\n   216\t    store.mark_step(conn, step_id(ticker, items[0]['publication_day']), seq, STEP, 'ok', json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False), coverage_start, at)\n   217\t    conn.commit()\n   218\t    log(f'--- coverage-start reading of {ticker}: {len(items)} report items, {len(readings)} readings, {len(records)} records linked to {changed}, '\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   169\t\n   170\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\n   171\t1. Stored data: reproduce the failing case, show the fix flips it, show a mutant of the fix fails the check ($0).\n   172\t2. Only when what the model is asked changed: re-send just the affected calls.\n   173\t3. The touched suites, plus any standing structural checks the change can affect; the full suite once.\n   174\t4. The gate once, at merge (README, \"Build and check\"). The acceptance once, on the final configuration, scored on the frozen ruler\n   175\t   (§7.1). Never a full rerun per fix.\n   176\t\n   177\t- A further check the change does not need is offered in one line, not run. After the checks that prove a change pass, report and close.\n   178\t- To accept a code change, replay stored decisions through the code deterministically ($0); a sampler run proves nothing about code,\n   179\t  and a cached replay proves nothing about the model.\n   180\t- A re-sent request is the bytes production sends, not the archive's canonical JSON: `model.request_identity` sorts keys for the\n   181\t  archive, `model.call` sends the dict as built. Check a harness by comparing an answer's key order with a production answer's.\n   182\t- Before any paid run, `python3 scripts/preflight.py` replays the stored model answers and matching records of the archives and ledgers\n   183\t  it is given through the current code checks and prompts ($0; it skips rows an earlier run refused, so read what it says it skipped)\n   184\t  and prints, per check, the cases judged and the refusals with reasons (it does not yet replay the coverage-start reading's check:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md | cut -c1-1600; rg -n -m3 'sealed|views.sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round72b-brief.md; rg -n 'sealed|2026-10-28' README.md | head -n 12\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t1. **Revision 2 leaves a confirmed forecast leak through Yes/No answers.** In `old-3`, the August 25 explanation for a shipment question (`v36`, judgement 799) says that the 2027 spending forecast is “around $1 trillion.” In `old-1`, the August 28 explanation for the Firmus investment (`v10`, judgement 865) gives the selected band for **both** the 2026 and 2027 spending questions. I read both explanations through `service.history()`. The judge receives related questions’ selected bands and reasons, and history returns the resulting text. Revision 2 promises to return Yes/No records exactly as they are today. Those requirements conflict on stored data. Preserve the Yes/No outcome, and specify how release readers handle explanations that disclose another question’s forecast. Use these two records as acceptance cases. [Design:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:95) · [judging.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:208) · [service.py:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:263) · [bundle.py:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:120)\n     2\t\n     3\t2. **Identity works on the four stores if the Yes/No test uses the stored vocabulary.** I checked every question. The three comparison stores split into **19 number / 28 event**, **17 / 26**, and **18 / 31**. All 85 event questions have an `event` or `policy_event` measure. In the sealed ledger, 43 of 94 questions parse as money, 21 further number questions are safely withheld by the fallback, and 30 are Yes/No. All 30 use `是` and `否`. A literal English test would withhold all 30 incorrectly. Specify exactly two labels, canonicalized with the existing vocabulary, in either order. With that reading I found no wrong show-or-withhold result in the four stores. I also verified both round-72 counterexamples directly. Sealed revenue `v3` parses from its conditions. Xbox `v37` has the `growth_rate` measure and bounds around zero, but its two answers are explicitly Yes and No. [Design:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:30) · [identity.py:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [Xbox store manifest:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20)\n     4\t\n     5\t3. **The ambiguity rule still has a gap for a record with a key.** Section 2 limits its fallback to records with *no key*. The opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. I cleared only the bounds on an in-memory copy of `old-1/v8` and ran its five original English conditions through the service parser. All five were refused. The `segment_revenue` key still exists, so this supported shape reaches no stated outcome. Withhold and list every unresolved record, whether or not it has a key. That closes the gap without extending the money parser to every language and unit. [Design:34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:34) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [service.py:422](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:422) · [service.py:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499)\n     6\t\n     7\t4. **The idea card has a second path that restores hidden bands.** Revision 2 covers candidate summaries, related questions, evaluation, and `/ideas` with either bundle setting. But the configured idea-summary version reads the ladder directly from storage when building its answer format, and the summary call adds it to the input again. I passed `v8` through that helper with its judgement removed. It added back “at least $400 billion” and “less than $250 billion.” Exclude withheld ladders from both reads and inspect the actual summary request in the test. A clean `judged` field alone does not establish that the idea prose is clean. [Design:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:69) · [poc-v118-idea.json:94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:94) · [idea.py:350](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:350) · [idea_composite.py:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:255) · [idea_composite.py:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:281)\n     8\t\n     9\t5. **The approved screen, `claim_position`, search ranking, processing dates, closing text, and fixed setting are addressed in the design.** The question page keeps the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” including amounts a source actually quoted. Evaluation returns only the marker. Assessment counts and dates are omitted, and a closing record can say “closed” without its final band. Search ranks possible outcomes without reading the selected one. The design also identifies the browser’s separate assessment-date sort and fixes the release setting at `withheld`. These provisions match Alex’s decision and the cited readers. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [Design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [Design:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [Design:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:81) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553)\n    10\t\n    11\t6. **The main exports are named, but a clean HTML file can reload unrestricted data.** The page opens its embedded snapshot, then automatically fetches `/library` from an API that defaults to `127.0.0.1:8788`. It replaces the snapshot after checking only that the response is a complete library. The idea page fetches its bundles from the same address. Since revision 2 explicitly leaves the existing POC setting open, a release HTML file opened beside that POC can show its forecasts. Bind the release page to the release service or have it refuse unrestricted responses. Apply the same content check to prepared JSON before embedding it. The static builder also embeds `--composite-trials` separately from the main dataset, and the translated `data.en.json` export retains judgement prose. Keep those inputs outside the release package unless checked. [Design:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:72) · [bootstrap.js:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:20) · [bootstrap.js:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:193) · [bootstrap.js:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [mock_translate.py:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:114)\n    12\t\n    13\t7. **The acceptance check selects the right question, but cannot prove the closing case as written.** `old-1/v8` has 75 judgements, 69 rows marked changed, and 9 actual moves between bands. Its only stored switch is `open=1, reason=created`. Round 72 generated the closing sentence by calling the formatter. There is no closing sentence on this question for the release page to hide. Keep `v8` for the page and same-sources check. Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real stored closing switch, and first verify that the unrestricted response exposes its final band. For the $0 idea check, use a recorded or test transport and inspect the composed request as well as the delivered card. [Design:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109) · [pull.py:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:11) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [service.py:356](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:356) · [idea.py:218](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:218)\n    14\t\n    15\t**Verdict — not ready.** An unchanged Yes/No explanation already discloses a number forecast in the stored data. Revision 2 needs to resolve that conflict and close the idea, identity, and export gaps before Alex opens release work. This review was read-only and cost $0.15:   - the identity rule's two counterexamples (sealed `v3`, Xbox `v37`);\n28:   Does it misclassify any question in the three comparison stores or the sealed ledger the tests use?\n93:| Collected thesis ledger | `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` |\n114:Then restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
