{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md | sed -n '1p;6,8p' | cut -c1-900; nl -ba src/hivemind/extraction.py | sed -n '387,414p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '115,125p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t1. **Revision 2 leaves a confirmed forecast leak through Yes/No answers.** In `old-3`, the August 25 explanation for a shipment question (`v36`, judgement 799) says that the 2027 spending forecast is “around $1 trillion.” In `old-1`, the August 28 explanation for the Firmus investment (`v10`, judgement 865) gives the selected band for **both** the 2026 and 2027 spending questions. I read both explanations through `service.history()`. The judge receives related questions’ selected bands and reasons, and history returns the resulting text. Revision 2 promises to return Yes/No records exactly as they are today. Those requirements conflict on stored data. Preserve the Yes/No outcome, and specify how release readers handle explanations that disclose another question’s forecast. Use these two records as acceptance cases. [Design:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-numb\n     6\t\n     7\t4. **The idea card has a second path that restores hidden bands.** Revision 2 covers candidate summaries, related questions, evaluation, and `/ideas` with either bundle setting. But the configured idea-summary version reads the ladder directly from storage when building its answer format, and the summary call adds it to the input again. I passed `v8` through that helper with its judgement removed. It added back “at least $400 billion” and “less than $250 billion.” Exclude withheld ladders from both reads and inspect the actual summary request in the test. A clean `judged` field alone does not establish that the idea prose is clean. [Design:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:69) · [poc-v118-idea.json:94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:94) · [idea.py:350](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/id\n     8\t\n   387\t    fiscal = '\\n'.join(note for note in (universe.fiscal_note(o, item['publication_day'], english=True) for o in objects) if note)\n   388\t    parts = [\n   389\t        f'[Category and how to read it] {category}. {blocks[\"what\"]}',\n   390\t        f'[Subjects] The objects this item concerns: {\", \".join(objects) or \"(not labelled upstream)\"}. For a candidate thesis about a company, object is its ticker; '\n   391\t        f'about a theme, choose an id from this list, or state what the matter is when none fits:\\n{themes}'\n   392\t        + (f'\\nFiscal-year note (a numeric thesis takes its year and due date from it):\\n{fiscal}' if fiscal else ''),\n   393\t        f'[What to read out] {blocks[\"read\"]}',\n   394\t    ]\n   395\t    watched = _watched_lines(objects, universe)\n   396\t    if watched:\n   397\t        parts.append('[Research reference] Existing quantities and scopes (measure[scope](event_type)). Reuse a name only when the meaning is the same; '\n   398\t                     'propose important questions outside the list as usual, with their actual scope:\\n' + '\\n'.join(watched))\n   399\t    lines = placement.question_lines(shown_views)\n   400\t    parts.append(f'[Open questions at the start of {item[\"publication_day\"]}]\\n' + ('\\n'.join(lines) if lines else '  None yet.'))\n   401\t    parts.append(GROUPS_INSTRUCTION)\n   402\t    parts.append(item_header(item, category) + text[:MAX_TEXT_CHARS])\n   403\t    parts.append(CLOSING)\n   404\t    parts.append(_read(f'review-{version}.txt').strip())\n   405\t    return _read(f'role-{version}.txt'), '\\n\\n'.join(parts)\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\tOBJECT_LABELS = vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS\n   409\t\n   410\t\n   411\tdef check_ladder(rungs, kind):\n   412\t    \"\"\"None when the ladder is well formed, else the problem. An asset ladder written from Strongly bearish up to\n   413\t    Strongly bullish (the model often orders a revenue ladder by rising value) is the same ladder; normalise_ladder\n   414\t    turns it round. Labels are compared in the canonical vocabulary.\"\"\"\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   117\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n   118\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n   119\t  question, not something to build.\n   120\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n   121\t\n   122\t## 3. Writing code\n   123\t\n   124\t- **One owner.** A rule lives where the data is written, and refuses: a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure. Fix the\n   125\t  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
